<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Elchingen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1805">1805</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-third-coalition">War of the Third Coalition</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elchingen">Elchingen</a> was fought on 14 October 1805 near Ulm in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swabia-bavaria">Swabia</a> during the Ulm campaign of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-third-coalition">War of the Third Coalition</a>. French troops under Marshal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/michel-ney">Michel Ney</a> forced the crossing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> and stormed the heights of Elchingen, defeating an Austrian corps under Johann Sigismund Riesch. The victory helped encircle General Mack's army at Ulm, and Ney was later made Duke of Elchingen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-elchingen.jpg" alt="Battle of Elchingen" width="320" height="194" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Lorenz Rugendas · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Elchingen_in_1805_(J._L._Rugendas_II).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
